<main id="main-content" tabindex="-1" class="v2-reference"><article><header class="article-top"><div class="article-intro"><a class="article-back" href="<?= e(url('/care-guide')) ?>">← <span>Back to the care notes</span></a><p class="eyebrow">THE ESSENTIALS</p><h1>A wash day with a little more clarity.</h1><p>Start with a simple order. Then let your scalp, texture, and product directions guide the details.</p><span class="article-meta">AVELA CARE NOTES · 2 MIN READ</span></div><div class="article-visual"><?= handoff_guide_art('cleanse') ?></div></header><div class="article-body"><nav class="article-outline" aria-label="In this note"><p class="eyebrow">IN THIS NOTE</p><a href="#note-0">Start at the scalp.</a><a href="#note-1">Follow with conditioning.</a></nav><div class="article-copy"><section id="note-0"><h2>Start at the scalp.</h2><p>Apply shampoo to your scalp and massage gently. As you rinse, let the shampoo flow through your lengths, without scrubbing them together.</p></section><section id="note-1"><h2>Follow with conditioning.</h2><p>Condition after washing. Your hair type can help guide where you apply it: the ends for fine or straight hair, and along the lengths for dry or curly hair.</p></section><div class="article-takeaway"><span class="eyebrow">A LITTLE TAKEAWAY</span><p>Avela does not assign a fixed wash calendar. Notice when your scalp feels dirty or oily, and follow your product directions.</p></div><div class="article-reference">Care reference<br><a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/hair-scalp-care/hair/healthy-hair-tips" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">American Academy of Dermatology · Tips for healthy hair</a><p>General cosmetic care guidance. Avela does not diagnose or treat hair or scalp conditions.</p></div></div></div></article><section class="guide-cta"><div><h2>Make a little room for you.</h2><p>Bring what you know about your hair into your own routine.</p></div><a class="button primary" href="<?= e(url('/assessment')) ?>">Build my hair profile </a></section></main>
